  "goodToKnow": "Der Rechnungshof is a court of audit that checks public spending. The Bundesrechnungshof in Bonn audits federal finances, and each state has its own Landesrechnungshof; their members are independent like judges. Its reports often criticise waste. Not to be confused with the Schwarzbuch, an annual list of wasted tax money from the lobby group Bund der Steuerzahler. Plural: die Rechnungshöfe."
